// Comparing against NaN.
//
// No ordering accepts NaN, and `@float.cmp` has three answers, none of which
// is true of it. Reporting one would be claiming a relation the format denies,
// so it refuses — here while compiling, and as a trap in a program where the
// value only shows up at run time. `@int.div` by zero takes the same two
// shapes.
//
// `Float.is_nan` is the question that does have an answer, and asking it first
// is what `examples/floats.blot` does. It is a primitive for exactly this
// reason: comparing is what refuses, so nothing written over `Float.cmp` could
// have reported it.

open import "blot:prelude"

let nothing = Float.div 0.0 0.0

return is_less (Float.cmp nothing 1.0)
